From e894b27e3df7833260bc2a423121caf213117e8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:15:37 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] A file to another of the person's computers moves to the
 direct link when it comes up

A message's files picked their road once per attempt. A 2.1 MB image sent
while pairing was 0.84 s from done started on the relay and stayed there
for all of its 21.7 s, though the direct link was up for nearly all of it.

- push_attachments asks Roads for the road each time the window has room
  for more chunks, not once per attempt. A file under way on the relay
  moves to the direct link as soon as that comes up, and back if it drops.
  The host keeps each chunk whichever road carried it (UploadChunk is
  idempotent per seq), and the commit takes the road picked last.
- A transfer of 256 KiB or more waits up to 1.5 s for a pairing already
  under way (Links::client_within, Roads::client_within) instead of
  starting on the relay. Nothing under way, or a failure a moment ago: the
  relay at once, as before.
- A file attached in a chat's composer gets the link to that chat's host
  ready before Send: the composer calls chat.warm_link, zgx calls the
  engine's new local-only WarmDeviceLink {chatId | deviceId} -> {warming},
  and Roads::warm pairs, opens the rpc stream and keeps an open one from
  closing as idle (Links::warm_link, one at a time per device, never to a
  Cloud machine). An engine without it answers unknown method and the
  first call pairs as before.

Tests: flaky_link_attachments'
a_big_file_waits_a_moment_for_a_pairing_under_way_and_goes_direct and
a_file_on_the_relay_moves_to_the_direct_link_when_it_comes_up (a stand-in
pairing in front of B's real direct host); direct_rpc's
a_pairing_under_way_is_waited_for_a_moment and
a_link_warmed_ahead_is_up_for_the_first_call; zgx's
chat_warm_link.test.luau.
